      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "School vouchers are viewed positively by some as they provide families with the ability to choose the best educational opportunities for their children, promoting competition and potentially improving educational outcomes. Critics argue that vouchers divert public funds from already under-resourced public schools, exacerbate inequities, and may result in a two-tiered education system where public schools suffer from reduced resources and support. The debate hinges on balancing school choice with ensuring that all children have equal access to quality education.",
